# The bucket's keys: copy to <site>/secrets/s3.env (k8s/up.sh makes Secret "s3", which Ghost's storage adapter signs
# in with). gke: the HMAC key of a service account with Storage Object User on the bucket. eks needs none (Ghost's
# role, GHOST_ROLE_ARN in cloud-eks.env). Overlays with the in-cluster S3 gateway (local, the k3d twins) make their
# own when this file isn't there.

# The HMAC key: its access ID (GOOG...) and its secret (Cloud Storage's S3 API takes them as AWS-style keys)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=GOOG1EXAMPLE
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
